#reference: Sputtered Energy Coefficient and Sputtering Yield, Wolfgang Eckstein, IPP-report-17/29-December,2011
##these fitting parameters are used for computing Sputtered energy coefficient
#fitting parameters for Eckstein physical sputtering yield.
#the fitting formular is valid when: for low mass ions, the maximum incident energy is 20keV
##for heavy ions, the maximum incident energy is 200keV. 
#for each material, and each incident species, the fitting parameters for different incident species are different.
##:first column: incident species name;
##:second column: target species name;
##:third column: lambda;
##:fourth column: q;
##:fifth column: mu;
##:sixth column: the threshold energy;
##:seventh column: nu.
##:eighth column: the energy at Lindhard screening length(\varepsilon_L)
##:ninth column: the surface binding energy 
##:n: the exponential term of Sn_KrC(2 for light ions(H->He), 1 for heavy ions(O->... and selfbombardment)))

H   W   6.453   1.202e-5    3.302   392.0   1.141   9.86986e3   8.68    2
D   W   3.665   1.000e-4    2.279   229.743 1.210   9.92326e3   8.68    2
T   W   4.524   1.000e-4    2.436   152.506 1.250   9.97718e3   8.68    2
O   W   13.08   1.400e-3    2.370   44.105  1.820   9.19794e4   8.68    1
Ar  W   48.69   3.400e-3    3.105   26.501  1.803   2.46646e5   8.68    1
W   W   2.983e3 3.000e-3    3.363   18.144  1.839   1.99860e6   8.68    1